def esc(x):return html.escape(str(x))
def table(head,rows):return '<table><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+esc(x)+'</th>' for x in head)+'</tr>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(x)+'</td>' for x in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</table>'
stems=read(OUT/'data/figure_stems.json')+['aspergillus_evodevo_gates'];save(OUT/'data/figure_stems.json',stems)
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Type-qualified phylogenies and Aspergillus evo-devo gates</title><style>body{font:15px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:1450px;margin:35px auto;padding:0 25px;color:#203849}h1,h2,h3{color:#24596c}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px;margin:18px 0}th,td{padding:9px;border:1px solid #ccd7de;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#e9f1f5}tr:nth-child(even){background:#f5f8fa}a{color:#006c87}.lead{background:#e9f1f5;padding:18px}</style>'''
page+='<h1>Type-qualified core and three-gene phylogenies</h1><p>20 November 2026 | new figure release; original trees and active scientific jobs preserved.</p>'
page+='<p class="lead">All 66 core tips map to the current complete three-gene tree. The requested type-exclusive monophyly rule changes 31 reported core-tip species labels. Of the 66 assignments, 42 have enclosing-clade SH-aLRT >=80 and UFBoot >=95; 24 are topology-only assignments (22 A. terreus and 2 A. alabamensis). These confidence classes are separate in every plot.</p>'
page+='<h2>Figures</h2><ul>'+''.join('<li>'+esc(s.replace('_',' '))+': <a href="figures/'+s+'.pdf">single-page vector PDF</a> | <a href="figures/'+s+'.png">300 dpi PNG</a></li>' for s in stems)+'</ul>'
page+='<h2>Definition and interpretation</h2><p>'+esc(summary['rule'])+'</p><p>'+esc(summary['support_rule'])+'</p><p>'+esc(summary['core_transfer_rule'])+'</p><p>Reported non-type labels can be wrong and therefore do not veto the type-based assignment. Conflicting non-type reference labels are listed explicitly in the clade audit. This procedure identifies type-containing groups within this sampled topology; it is not an independent formal species-delimitation or nomenclatural revision.</p>'
page+='<p><b>Monophyly is not the same as support:</b> the enclosing A. terreus clade has SH-aLRT 33.5 / UFBoot 61; A. alabamensis has 90.9 / 89. Their labels carry an asterisk and an amber support cell. The smaller well-supported A. alabamensis subset from the older annotation is not silently substituted for the maximal type-exclusive clade.</p>'
page+='<p><b>Cross-tree discordance:</b> the transferred A. montoensis and A. terreus groups are not monophyletic in the current core topology. Their core tips retain the requested three-gene-derived labels, but brown Core cells mark the conflict and right-hand species names repeat across separate pure blocks. No mixed core clade is renamed wholesale. Other multi-tip assigned core groups pass the unrooted split check; singleton groups provide no multi-tip monophyly test.</p>'
page+='<p><b>A. neoterreus:</b> its five-reference clade is labelled in the three-gene plot (SH-aLRT 92.6 / UFBoot 96), but it contains no genome-derived entry in this current dataset. No core genome is assigned that name by this rule.</p>'
page+='<p><b>Type sampling:</b> the A. jilinensis and A. ralucae type references lack complete three-locus representation and are excluded from complete230. Assignments are conditional on the included types; this analysis cannot exclude every unsampled sister taxon. Resolving those missing type loci is part of E1.</p>'
page+=table(['Assigned species','Core tips','Evidence'],[(r['species'],r['count'],r['confidence']) for r in summary['core_assignments']])
page+='<h2>Core-tip audit</h2>'+table(['Genome','Reported species','Type-derived species','Evidence','Core monophyly'],[(r['sample'],r['reported_species'],r['assigned_species'],r['confidence'],r['core_monophyly']) for r in audit if r['in_core66']])
page+='<h2>Type anchors and boundaries</h2>'+table(['Species','Type culture(s)','All tips / genomes / core tips','SH-aLRT / UFBoot','Non-type reference name conflicts'],[(g['species'],'; '.join(g.get('anchor_cultures',[])),f"{len(g['tips'])} / {len(g.get('genome_tips',[]))} / {len(g.get('core_tips',[]))}",str(g.get('SH_aLRT'))+' / '+str(g.get('UFBoot')),'; '.join(x['tip']+': '+x['reported_reference_species'] for x in g.get('conflicting_non_type_reference_labels',[]))) for g in clades])
page+='<h2>Way forward: adapt the Klebsiella evo-devo concept</h2><p>The transferable framework is evidence-qualified evolutionary comparative genomics: define independent units and measured endpoints; establish ancestry; validate characters; describe population ecology; fit suitable evolutionary models; then test associations and independent usefulness. In Aspergillus, replace bacterial gene/clone assumptions with intron-aware fungal orthology, paralog/copy-number checks and biosynthetic-cluster architecture. Developmental claims need actual developmental phenotypes; gene presence alone is not a developmental assay.</p>'
page+='<p>The immediate pilot should focus on the lovastatin cluster: intact/disrupted/duplicated gene states, flanking synteny and callability across the current taxa. Add measured production or expression only when assay conditions and units are linked. Use the WT/sector pair as a matched contrast. New CMI 44339 and 59TF downloads are staged candidates and are not included in these current-tree figures.</p>'
for g in gates:
 page+='<h3>'+esc(g['gate'])+'</h3><p><b>Current status:</b> '+esc(g['status'])+' Existing execution gates: '+esc(g['existing_gates'])+'.</p>'
 for title,key in [('Input data','inputs'),('Method','method'),('Pass criterion','pass_rule'),('Return','output'),('Benefit','benefit')]:page+='<p><b>'+title+':</b> '+esc(g[key])+'</p>'
page+='<h2>Prioritised deliverables</h2><ol><li>Freeze the sample/type map and resolve A. terreus/A. montoensis backbone discordance.</li><li>Produce a callable Lov gene/cluster matrix and lineage-stratified architecture heatmap.</li><li>Only after backbone and character gates pass, fit alternative ancestral histories with uncertainty.</li><li>Test lineage-adjusted links to measured phenotypes and use the WT/sector contrast to prioritise mechanisms.</li><li>Validate key claims independently; do not infer a production phenotype from cluster presence or transfer from discordance alone.</li></ol>'
page+='<h2>Provenance and limits</h2><p>'+esc(summary['rooting_note'])+' All 2,145 pairwise core distances and unrooted splits were checked after display rerooting. Original ML branch lengths are retained in linear views; circular and matched comparison views are cladograms. The full 230-tip reference tree remains the assignment source, rather than a reference-free 66-tip reconstruction.</p><p>The latest completed release inputs were core66 and complete230; no newer completed core tree was found in the gate execution runs. BUSCO/QC work continues independently. New downloads are not silently incorporated. Source hashes, mappings and machine-readable gates are provided below.</p>'
page+='<p><a href="data/analysis_summary.json">Method and input hashes</a> | <a href="data/assignment_audit.json">All 230 tip assignments</a> | <a href="data/type_monophyly_clades.json">Type/clade evidence</a> | <a href="data/rooting_validation.json">Rooting verification</a> | <a href="data/evodevo_gates.json">Full gates</a> | <a href="data/evodevo_concept_sources.json">Reviewed Klebsiella sources</a>.</p>'
page+='<p>The three-gene source run used IQ-TREE 2.4.0, partitioned MFP+MERGE, 1,000 UFBoot and 1,000 SH-aLRT replicates, -bnni, seed 20261118, and A. flavipes NRRL302 as the specified outgroup. No ML inference was rerun for this annotation release.</p>'
page+='<p>Method sources: <a href="https://www.iqtree.org/doc/Concordance-Factor">IQ-TREE gene/site concordance</a>; <a href="https://phytools.org/static.help/make.simmap.html">phytools stochastic mapping</a>; <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10773453/">phytools 2.0</a>; <a href="https://fungismash.secondarymetabolites.org/">fungal antiSMASH</a>. These support proposed methods; they are not evidence that those downstream analyses have been run.</p></html>'
(OUT/'review.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
(OUT/'README.txt').write_text('TYPE-QUALIFIED PHYLOGENIES | 20 November 2026\n\nOpen review.html for all figures, the core-tip species audit, type anchors and the proposed Aspergillus evo-devo gates.\nEach PDF is one page; PDFs and SVGs are vector output. PNGs are rendered at 300 dpi.\n31 of 66 reported core labels change under the defined type-exclusive monophyly rule; 42 assignments have strong clade support and 24 remain topology-only. A. montoensis and A. terreus do not form single monophyletic groups in the current core tree, and are flagged rather than forced into agreement. No core entry falls in the A. neoterreus reference clade.\nOriginal analyses and active jobs were not modified. The new genome downloads remain staged and are not included here.\n',encoding='utf-8')
